      "chars/token is ~constant across ALL rungs (see chars_per_token_realized), so within a target 'character position' and 'token index' are proportional. A K that is constant across rungs is therefore equally consistent with (C) a fixed token-index scan AND with a fixed-ABSOLUTE-CAPACITY reading of (A) bandwidth. The pre-registered mapping calls it (C); what the data strictly supports is 'the collapse point is invariant to page density', which rules out a density-proportional bandwidth account but not a fixed-capacity one. Extra leverage: if a short rung whose ENTIRE page fits inside the implied capacity still collapses at the same position, fixed-capacity is excluded.",
      "The position-0 profile is the primary discriminator here BECAUSE K is undefined on any rung that never reads. It is not itself pre-registered; it is the pre-registered logic (does the collapse point move with density?) evaluated at the one position every rung can supply. Its weakness is the mirror image of K's: it says nothing about what happens deeper in the page, so a rung that reads position 0 and nothing else scores the same as one that reads throughout. Read it together with the per-position tables.",
